APPR-6146	EXECUTION	fc4f8732-4cf7-4937-8b74-ea814cfb56bc	Incident	The dashboard service on Worker1 (192.168.56.10) is reported as down. This SOP covers systematic diagnosis of the hosting process (systemd or container runtime), resource exhaustion, port binding conflicts, and log analysis to restore service availability. Resolution typically involves service restart, container recreation, or resource cleanup.	Execute SSH Remediation	85	REJECTED	2026-08-04 21:14:02.975	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "agentId": "agent-unix-resolver-01", "kbTitle": "SOP: Troubleshoot Dashboard Service Unavailability on Linux Worker Node", "targetCi": "Worker 1 (192.168.56.10)", "agentName": "🤖 Unix Auto-Resolver Agent", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "Dashboard unavailability on a generic Linux worker typically stems from: 1) Service crash (OOM kill, config error, dependency failure), 2) Container runtime issues (image pull failure, volume mount corruption, restart loop), 3) Resource exhaustion (disk full on /var/lib/docker or /var/lib/grafana, memory pressure), or 4) Network stack issues (port conflict, firewall drop). The steps prioritize non-intrusive discovery (ss, ps, systemctl, docker/crictl) before taking corrective actions (restart). Idempotent checks (systemctl is-active, docker ps -q) prevent errors if the service is managed differently than assumed. Verification uses local curl to isolate network path issues from application health.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "Verify target server IP (192.168.56.10) matches CMDB record for Worker1OL before executing SSH.", "passed": true}, {"check": "Confirm maintenance window approval or stakeholder acknowledgment before restarting production dashboard services.", "passed": true}, {"check": "Ensure backup of persistent data volumes (Grafana /var/lib/grafana, Prometheus /prometheus) exists prior to container recreation or filesystem repair.", "passed": true}, {"check": "Validate that the dashboard service is managed by systemd OR container runtime, not both simultaneously (double-management causes port conflicts).", "passed": true}, {"check": "Check firewall rules (firewalld/iptables/nftables) and SELinux/AppArmor audit logs if service binds locally but fails remote access.", "passed": true}], "incidentTitle": "Dashboard is down on Worker1OL server", "rejectionReason": "harmful commands", "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"echo '=== 1. Network Connectivity & Port Verification ==='\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"ss -tlnp | grep -E ':3000|:8080|:8443|:9090|:9443|:30000|:31000|:32000' || echo 'No common dashboard ports listening'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"echo '=== 2. Process & Service Discovery ==='\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"ps auxf | grep -iE 'grafana|prometheus|kibana|dashboard|node-exporter|dashy|homepage|portainer|rancher' | grep -v grep || echo 'No obvious dashboard processes found via ps'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running | grep -iE 'grafana|prometheus|kibana|dashboard|docker|containerd|crio|kubelet' || echo 'No matching systemd services running'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"systemctl list-units --type=service --state=failed | grep -iE 'grafana|prometheus|kibana|dashboard|docker|containerd|crio|kubelet' || echo 'No failed matching systemd units'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"echo '=== 3. Container Runtime Inspection (Docker/Containerd/CRI-O) ==='\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"which docker >/dev/null 2>&1 && docker ps -a --filter \\"name=grafana\\" --filter \\"name=prometheus\\" --filter \\"name=dashboard\\" --filter \\"name=kibana\\" --format \\"table {{.Names}}\\\\t{{.Status}}\\\\t{{.Ports}}\\\\t{{.Image}}\\" || echo 'Docker not found or no matching containers'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.56.10 \\"which crictl >/dev/null 2>&1 && crictl ps -a | grep -iE 'grafana|prometheus|dashboard|kibana' || echo 'CRICTL not found or no matching pods/containers'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.