APPR-9800	EXECUTION	4862e913-45f2-4391-ae57-99fc5a4995f7	Incident	Dirty page ratio exceeded threshold on control plane 192.168.100.101, indicating aggressive writeback pressure or misconfigured VM dirty limits. This SOP diagnoses the dirty page backlog, identifies offending writers, tunes vm.dirty_* sysctls for faster background writeback, and safely reclaims page cache to prevent OOM kills on critical control plane components (etcd, kube-apiserver, containerd).	Execute SSH Remediation	85	REJECTED	2026-08-06 23:58:08.504	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "SOP: Page Cache Overflow & Memory Exhaustion Mitigation on Control Plane", "summary": "Dirty page ratio exceeded threshold on control plane 192.168.100.101, indicating aggressive writeback pressure or misconfigured VM dirty limits. This SOP diagnoses the dirty page backlog, identifies offending writers, tunes vm.dirty_* sysctls for faster background writeback, and safely reclaims page cache to prevent OOM kills on critical control plane components (etcd, kube-apiserver, containerd).", "targetCi": "Control Plane (192.168.100.101)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "Dirty page overflow occurs when application write throughput exceeds background writeback capacity, pinning memory as unreclaimable page cache. Default vm.dirty_ratio=20 and vm.dirty_background_ratio=10 allow up to 20% of RAM as dirty pages before blocking writers, which on 64GB+ systems equals 12GB+ of stuck memory. Reducing ratios to 15/5 and shortening expire/writeback intervals forces earlier pdflush/kworker writeback, preventing synchronous write stalls. The sync; echo 1 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches safely reclaims clean page cache after flushing. Persistent sysctl config prevents regression. Process and I/O inspection identifies if etcd WAL, containerd snapshotters, or log spam drive the write amplification.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "Verify MemAvailable > 20% of MemTotal after cache drop and 