APPR-4375	EXECUTION	2553f784-8b0c-4e53-9170-4d1f98bae5b8	Incident	High CPU on control plane nodes typically stems from kube-apiserver request storms (e.g., watch leaks, misconfigured informers), etcd compaction/defrag cycles, or runaway controller-manager reconciliation loops. This SOP isolates the offending process via PID mapping, validates etcd health, and applies targeted mitigation (restart of specific static pod) without full node reboot.	Execute SSH Remediation	85	REJECTED	2026-08-07 00:10:42.664	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "SOP: High CPU Utilization on Kubernetes Control Plane Node", "summary": "High CPU on control plane nodes typically stems from kube-apiserver request storms (e.g., watch leaks, misconfigured informers), etcd compaction/defrag cycles, or runaway controller-manager reconciliation loops. This SOP isolates the offending process via PID mapping, validates etcd health, and applies targeted mitigation (restart of specific static pod) without full node reboot.", "targetCi": "Control Plane (192.168.100.101)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "Control plane CPU spikes are rarely generic; they map to specific components. Step 1-4 identify the PID/container consuming CPU. Steps 5-6 map PIDs to component names and check kubelet/journal for OOM kills or throttling. Steps 7-8 inspect component logs for watch leaks, audit webhook timeouts, or etcd slow applies. Steps 9-10 verify etcd quorum and alarms (critical before restarts). Step 11 confirms kubelet health. Step 12 checks if static pods lack CPU limits (common root cause). Step 13 shows per-container usage. Steps 14-16 perform graceful restarts of offending static pods via crictl (kubelet will restart them immediately with same spec). Step 17 validates mitigation. Step 18 confirms all control plane pods are Running. Restarting via crictl is safer than systemctl restart kubelet (which cycles all pods).", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "Verify etcd cluster health (endpoint status) before restarting any control plane component to avoid quorum loss", "passed": true}, {"check": "Confirm kubelet is running and managing static pods before issuing crictl stop commands", "passed": true}, {"check": "Ensure no active leadership elections are disrupted (check logs for 'leader elected' messages post-restart)", "passed": true}, {"check": "Validate API server responsiveness post-restart: 'kubectl get nodes --request-timeout=5s' from a healthy node or local admin kubeconfig", "passed": true}, {"check": "Check CPU returns to baseline (< 70% sustained) for 10 minutes before closing ticket", "passed": true}], "incidentTitle": "High CPU Utilization on Control Plane", "confidenceScore": 85, "rejectionReason": "skipping", "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"top -b -n 1 | head -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ps aux --sort=-%cpu | head -15\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl ps --sort-by cpu --no-trunc | head -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl top | head -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"for pid in $(pgrep -f 'kube-apiserver|kube-controller-manager|kube-scheduler|etcd'); do echo \\"--- PID $pid ---\\"; cat /proc/$pid/cmdline | xargs -0 echo; done\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"journalctl -u kubelet --since '30 min ago' -p err..crit --no-pager | tail -30\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --name kube-apiserver -q) --tail=100 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'WARN|ERROR|panic|throttle' | tail -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --name etcd -q) --tail=100 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'apply took|slow|compaction|defrag' | tail -10\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key endpoint status --write-out=table\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernet