APPR-3959	EXECUTION	3d6987ce-3bbc-4117-aa83-784e29c8c291	Incident	This SOP addresses high memory pressure on a Kubernetes control plane node (192.168.100.101). The failure mode typically involves etcd database bloat, kube-apiserver cache growth, or container runtime memory leaks leading to OOM kills or eviction pressure. The resolution identifies the top memory consumers via crictl/systemd, performs targeted restarts of affected control plane components, and compacts etcd if database size exceeds quota.	Execute SSH Remediation	85	REJECTED	2026-08-07 00:12:46.065	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "SOP: High Memory Utilization Remediation on Kubernetes Control Plane Node", "summary": "This SOP addresses high memory pressure on a Kubernetes control plane node (192.168.100.101). The failure mode typically involves etcd database bloat, kube-apiserver cache growth, or container runtime memory leaks leading to OOM kills or eviction pressure. The resolution identifies the top memory consumers via crictl/systemd, performs targeted restarts of affected control plane components, and compacts etcd if database size exceeds quota.", "targetCi": "Control Plane (192.168.100.101)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "Control plane memory exhaustion is most frequently caused by etcd DB growth (triggering NOSPACE alarms), kube-apiserver watch cache bloat, or container runtime (containerd/crio) memory fragmentation. The procedure first quantifies memory pressure via free/ps/crictl, checks for OOM kills in logs, and inspects etcd quota/alarms. Immediate mitigation involves dropping clean page caches (safe), rolling restart of static pod containers (kube-apiserver, controller-manager, scheduler) to release heap memory, and etcd compaction/defrag to reclaim physical disk space and reduce memory mapping overhead. Container runtime restart is a last-resort step for runtime leaks. All commands are idempotent and use standard Kubernetes/RHEL tooling paths.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "Verify control plane pods (kube-apiserver, kube-controller-manager, kube-scheduler, etcd) are in 'Running' state via 'crictl ps' or 'kubectl get pods -n kube-system' from a healthy node.", "passed": true}, {"check": "Confirm etcd cluster health: 'ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl endpoint health --cluster --cacert=... --cert=... --key=...' returns healthy for all members.", "passed": true}, {"check": "Ensure node Ready condition: 'kubectl get node 192.168.100.101' shows Ready=True and MemoryPressure=False.", "passed": true}, {"check": "Validate no OOMKill events in 'dmesg -T | grep -i oom' or 'journalctl -k | grep -i oom' post-remediation.", "passed": true}], "incidentTitle": "High Memory Utilization on Control Plane", "confidenceScore": 85, "rejectionReason": "skipping", "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"free -h && echo '---' && cat /proc/meminfo | grep -E 'MemTotal|MemAvailable|SwapTotal|SwapFree'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ps aux --sort=-%mem | head -n 20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl stats --no-trunc 2>/dev/null | sort -k 3 -hr | head -n 15\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running 'kube*' 'etcd*' 'containerd*' 'crio*' 'docker*' | grep -v '^UNIT'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"for svc in kubelet containerd crio docker; do systemctl status $svc --no-pager -l 2>/dev/null | head -n 5; done\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"journalctl -u kubelet -u containerd -u crio -u docker --since '1 hour ago' --no-pager | grep -i -e oom -e kill -e memory -e evict | tail -n 20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"if command -v etcdctl &> /dev/null; then ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key endpoint status --write-out=table 2>/dev/null; fi\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"if command -v etcdctl &> /dev/null; then ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key alarm list 2>/dev/null; fi\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ls -lh /var/lib/etcd/member/snap/ 2>/dev/null | head -n 5\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"sync && echo 3 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches && free -h\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl ps --name kube-apiserver -q 2>/dev/null | xargs -r crictl stop -t 30 2>/dev/null && sleep 5 && crictl ps --name kube-apiserver -q 2>/dev/null | xargs -r crictl start 2>/dev/null\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl ps --name kube-controller-manager -q 2>/dev/null | xargs -r crictl stop -t 30 2>/dev/null && sleep 5 && crictl ps --name kube-controller-manager -q 2>/dev/null | xargs -r crictl start 2>/dev/null\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl ps --name kube-scheduler -q 2>/dev/null | xargs -r crictl stop -t 30 2>/dev/null && sleep 5 && crictl ps --name kube-scheduler -q 2>/dev/null | xargs -r crictl start 2>/dev/null\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"if command -v etcdctl &> /dev/null; then ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key compact $(ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key endpoint status --write-out=json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '.[0].Status.header.revision') 2>/dev/null && ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key defrag 2>/dev/null; fi\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"systemctl restart containerd 2>/dev/null || systemctl restart crio 2>/dev/null || systemctl restart docker 2>/dev/null\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"slee