APPR-3706	EXECUTION	62dfdb91-d73f-493f-82e3-c398fe51d372	Incident	100% CPU saturation on a Kubernetes control plane node typically originates from kube-apiserver (unbounded list/watch requests or admission webhook latency), kube-controller-manager (garbage collection thrashing), or etcd (disk I/O wait manifesting as CPU sys/iowait). This SOP provides a structured diagnostic flow to identify the offending process, correlate with Kubernetes component logs, and apply targeted remediation without restarting the control plane quorum unnecessarily.	Execute SSH Remediation	85	REJECTED	2026-08-07 01:11:07.537	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "SOP: Control Plane Node High CPU Utilization Diagnosis and Remediation", "summary": "100% CPU saturation on a Kubernetes control plane node typically originates from kube-apiserver (unbounded list/watch requests or admission webhook latency), kube-controller-manager (garbage collection thrashing), or etcd (disk I/O wait manifesting as CPU sys/iowait). This SOP provides a structured diagnostic flow to identify the offending process, correlate with Kubernetes component logs, and apply targeted remediation without restarting the control plane quorum unnecessarily.", "targetCi": "control plane (192.168.100.101)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "Control plane CPU saturation is rarely generic; it maps to specific component pathologies. kube-apiserver spikes usually correlate with high-cardinality resource watches (e.g., unfiltered List calls from broken controllers) or admission webhook timeouts causing request queue buildup (visible via apiserver_current_inflight_requests). kube-controller-manager CPU often stems from garbage collector thrashing on orphaned resources or excessive reconcile loops. etcd presents as high sys/iowait due to fsync latency on slow disks or quota alarms blocking writes. The workflow prioritizes non-invasive diagnostics (pidstat, crictl stats, metrics endpoint) over restarts. Restarting kubelet (which manages static pods) is the safest remediation lever as it gracefully recreates static pods without touching etcd quorum. Journald vacuum prevents log-induced CPU spikes from forwarder backpressure. Audit log backend blocking is a known silent CPU killer on apiserver.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "Verify etcd cluster health and member list shows all members 'started=true' before any component restart", "passed": true}, {"check": "Confirm control plane node is cordoned/drained (kubectl cordon <node>; kubectl drain <node> --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data --force) if workload pods are scheduled on it", "passed": true}, {"check": "Ensure no active leadership migrations in progress (check kube-controller-manager/scheduler logs for 'leader elected') before restarting static pods", "passed": true}, {"check": "Validate /etc/kubernetes/manifests/ backups exist before modifying static pod manifests", "passed": true}, {"check": "Check disk space on /var/lib/etcd > 20% free and inodes available to rule out etcd compaction stalls", "passed": true}], "incidentTitle": "CPU utilization is 100 % on ControlPlane node", "confidenceScore": 85, "rejectionReason": "skipping", "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"top -bn1 | head -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"pidstat -u -p ALL 1 5 | awk '$8 ~ /kube|etcd|containerd|docker|crio/ {print}'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ps -eo pid,ppid,cmd,%cpu,%mem --sort=-%cpu | head -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl ps -a --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-apiserver 2>/dev/null || crictl ps -a | grep kube-apiserver\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl stats --no-stream 2>/dev/null | sort -k3 -hr | head -10\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"systemctl status kubelet --no-pager -l\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"journalctl -u kubelet --since '30 min ago' --no-pager | grep -E '(error|fail|warn|cpu|throttl)' | tail -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-apiserver -q 2>/dev/null | head -1) --tail=200 2>/dev/null | grep -E '(error|panic|throttl|slow|timeout|watch.*duration)' | tail -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-controller-manager -q 2>/dev/null | head -1) --tail=200 2>/dev/null | grep -E '(error|panic|throttl|slow|timeout|garbage)' | tail -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-scheduler -q 2>/dev/null | head -1) --tail=100 2>/dev/null | grep -E '(error|panic|throttl|slow|timeout)' | tail -10\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"etcdctl endpoint status --cluster -w table 2>/dev/null || ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key endpoint status -w table\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key alarm list 2>/dev/null\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"grep -r 'request-timeout\\\\|watch-cache-size\\\\|max-requests-inflight' /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml 2>/dev/null || echo 'Manifest flags not found, checking defaults'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"df -h /var/lib/etcd /var/lib/kubelet /var/log\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"journalctl --vacuum-time=2d 2>/dev/null; systemctl reload systemd-journald 2>/dev/null\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"if pidstat -u -C kube-apiserver 1 1 | awk 'NR>3 {if ($8 > 80) exit 1}'; then echo 'kube-apiserver high CPU confirmed'; kubectl get --raw=/metrics 2>/dev/null | grep -E 'apiserver_request_duration_seconds|apiserver_current_inflight_requests' | head -5; fi\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"if grep -q 'audit-policy-file' /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-apiserver.yaml 2>/dev/null; then echo 'Audit logging enabled, checking backend latency'; ls -lh /var/log/kubernetes/audit*.log 2>/dev/null | head -5; fi\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"systemctl restart kubelet 2>/dev/null && sleep 10 && systemctl is-active kubelet || echo 'Kubelet restart attempted'\\""], "synthesizerOutput": {"kbTitle": "SOP: Control Plane Node High CPU Utilization Diagnosis and Remediation", "draftKbId": "KB-SOP-NEW", "trendInsight": "Synthesized SOP containing 18 resolution steps starting with SSH connection.", "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"top -bn1 | head -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"pidstat -u -p ALL 1 5 | awk '$8 ~ /kube|etcd|containerd|docker|crio/ {print}'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ps -eo pid,ppid,cmd,%cpu,%mem --sort=-%cpu | head -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl ps -a --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-apiserver 2>/dev/null || crictl ps -a | grep kube-apiserver\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl stats --no-stream 2>/dev/null | sort -k3 -hr | head -10\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"systemctl status kubelet --no-pager -l\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"journalctl -u kubelet --since '30 min ago' --no-pager | grep -E '(error|fail|warn|cpu|throttl)' | tail -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-apiserver -q 2>/dev/null | head -1) --tail=200 2>/dev/null | grep -E '(error|panic|throttl|slow|timeout|watch.*duration)' | tail -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-controller-manager -q 2>/dev/null | head -1) --tail=200 2>/dev/null | grep -E '(error|panic|throttl|slow|timeout|garbage)' | tail -20\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"crictl logs $(crictl ps --label io.kubernetes.component=kube-scheduler -q 2>/dev/null | head -1) --tail=100 2>/dev/null | grep -E '(error|panic|throttl|slow|timeout)' | tail -10\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"etcdctl endpoint status --cluster -w table 2>/dev/null || ETCDCTL_