APPR-1059	EXECUTION	2b9fcc29-4bc5-4a79-89e1-5cff3bacdbd6	Incident	This SOP covers the complete deprovisioning of OS-level accounts 'asha' and 'beaver' which were used for IBM DB2 TESTDB access on WorkerNode1HL. The procedure archives home directories, removes sudo privileges, deletes the user accounts, and validates removal. DB2-level privileges are implicitly revoked when OS accounts are deleted since DB2 uses OS authentication.	Execute SSH Remediation	8500	REJECTED	2026-08-08 05:21:22.473	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "SOP: Deprovision DB2 Users Asha and Beaver from WorkerNode1HL", "summary": "This SOP covers the complete deprovisioning of OS-level accounts 'asha' and 'beaver' which were used for IBM DB2 TESTDB access on WorkerNode1HL. The procedure archives home directories, removes sudo privileges, deletes the user accounts, and validates removal. DB2-level privileges are implicitly revoked when OS accounts are deleted since DB2 uses OS authentication.", "targetCi": "WorkerNode1HL (192.168.100.102)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "DB2 on Linux uses OS-level authentication (PAM). Deleting the OS users 'asha' and 'beaver' automatically revokes their database access to TESTDB. The 'beaver access on Linux container' reference indicates a second OS account requiring identical deprovisioning. Following the mandatory L2 offboarding procedure ensures audit compliance: home directories are archived before deletion, sudoers drop-in files are removed, and userdel -r -f forces removal even if processes linger. Post-deletion validation checks /etc/passwd, /etc/group, sudoers, and /home to prove no residual artifacts remain.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "Verify both users are not running active processes: 'ps -u asha -u beaver --no-headers | wc -l' returns 0", "passed": true}, {"check": "Confirm DB2 instance is not disrupted: 'su - db2inst1 -c \\"db2 list applications\\" 2>/dev/null | head -20' shows no sessions f