APPR-3581	EXECUTION	a60e0496-56d0-49a6-b582-ff9f5cff3a47	Incident	Diagnostic findings confirm target users (suorathycotic01-05) do not exist on control plane (192.168.100.101). The sudoers configuration shows default defaults but no existing rules for these accounts. Root cause: missing user accounts and missing sudoers delegation for passwordless 'su - oracle' execution. Remediation requires creating the 5 user accounts and deploying a sudoers drop-in file granting NOPASSWD access to /bin/su - oracle for the specified accounts.	Execute SSH Remediation	85	EXECUTED	2026-08-11 06:47:34.753	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "Master SOP: Create Service Accounts with Passwordless sudo for Oracle User Switch", "summary": "Diagnostic findings confirm target users (suorathycotic01-05) do not exist on control plane (192.168.100.101). The sudoers configuration shows default defaults but no existing rules for these accounts. Root cause: missing user accounts and missing sudoers delegation for passwordless 'su - oracle' execution. Remediation requires creating the 5 user accounts and deploying a sudoers drop-in file granting NOPASSWD access to /bin/su - oracle for the specified accounts.", "targetCi": "control plane (192.168.100.101)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "Live diagnostics show zero matches for suorathycotic01-05 in getent passwd, confirming accounts are absent. The oracle user query returned no output in the snippet but is referenced in the ticket; the sudoers file shows no existing rules for these accounts. The resolution creates users with home directories and bash shells, then deploys a dedicated sudoers.d fragment defining a command alias for '/bin/su - oracle' and granting NOPASSWD access to the five accounts. This follows least-privilege principle by restricting elevation to only the oracle user switch. Verification steps confirm user existence, sudoers syntax validity, and functional passwordless execution.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "getent passwd suorathycotic01 suorathycotic02 suorathycotic03 suorathycotic04 suorathycotic05", "passed": true}, {"check": "sudo -l -U suorathycotic01 | grep -E 'su.*oracle|NOPASSWD'", "passed": true}, {"check": "sudo -u suorathycotic01 sudo -n su - oracle -c 'whoami' 2>&1 | grep -q oracle && echo 'SUCCESS: Passwordless su - oracle works' || echo 'FAIL: Check sudoers syntax'", "passed": true}, {"check": "visudo -c", "passed": true}], "incidentTitle": "create 5 users suorathycotic01 to suorathycotic05 on controlplane node. With passwordless access to execute command - su - oracle", "confidenceScore": 85, "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"for i in {01..05}; do useradd -m -s /bin/bash suorathycotic$i; done\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"cat > /etc/sudoers.d/suorathycotic-oracle << 'EOF'\\n# Allow suorathycotic01-05 to run 'su - oracle' without password\\nCmnd_Alias ORACLE_SU = /bin/su - oracle\\nsuorathycotic01,suorathycotic02,suorathycotic03,suorathycotic04,suorathycotic05 ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: ORACLE_SU\\nEOF\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/suorathycotic-oracle\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"visudo -c -f /etc/sudoers.d/suorathycotic-oracle\\""], "synthesizerOutput": {"kbTitle": "Master SOP: Create Service Accounts with Passwordless sudo for Oracle User Switch", "draftKbId": "KB-SOP-NEW", "trendInsight": "Synthesized SOP containing 4 resolution steps starting with SSH connection.", "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"for i in {01..05}; do useradd -m -s /bin/bash suorathycotic$i; done\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"cat > /etc/sudoers.d/suorathycotic-oracle << 'EOF'\\n# Allow suorathycotic01-05 to run 'su - oracle' without password\\nCmnd_Alias ORACLE_SU = /bin/su - oracle\\nsuorathycotic01,suorathycotic02,suorathycotic03,suorathycotic04,suorathycotic05 ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: ORACLE_SU\\nEOF\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/suorathycotic-oracle\\""