ndly fix it", "confidenceScore": 85, "proposedCommands": ["ssh root@192.168.100.102 \\"dnf install -y python3-distutils\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.102 \\"az --version\\""], "synthesizerOutput": {"kbTitle": "Master SOP: Resolve Azure CLI ModuleNotFoundError for 'distutils' on CentOS Stream 10", "draftKbId": "KB-SOP-NEW", "trendInsight": "Synthesized SOP containing 2 resolution steps starting with SSH connection.", "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.102 \\"dnf install -y python3-distutils\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.102 \\"az --version\\""], "synthesizedSolution": "ssh root@192.168.100.102 \\"dnf install -y python3-distutils\\"\\nssh root@192.168.100.102 \\"az --version\\""}, "kbArticleReference": "KB_NEW"}
APPR-4147	EXECUTION	0a9b7727-5561-4a4e-813f-5b9b77402fcf	Incident	This SOP details the procedure to authenticate Azure CLI, identify the target Subscription and Cost Management Scope, and create a Budget resource via REST API (invoked via az cli) to trigger an alert notification when forecasted or actual costs exceed $5 USD. The procedure is executed locally on WorkerNode1HL (CentOS Stream 10) using the pre-installed Azure CLI v2.89.1.	Execute SSH Remediation	85	EXECUTED	2026-08-12 07:46:35.265	{"model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "kbTitle": "Master SOP: Configure Azure CLI Cost Management Budget Alert on Linux Worker Node", "summary": "This SOP details the procedure to authenticate Azure CLI, identify the target Subscription and Cost Management Scope, and create a Budget resource via REST API (invoked via az cli) to trigger an alert notification when forecasted or actual costs exceed $5 USD. The procedure is executed locally on WorkerNode1HL (CentOS Stream 10) using the pre-installed Azure CLI v2.89.1.", "targetCi": "WorkerNode1HL (192.168.100.102)", "riskLevel": "HIGH", "department": "DevOps Team", "aiReasoning": "The target node (WorkerNode1HL) runs CentOS Stream 10 with Azure CLI 2.89.1 pre-installed. Since the `az consumption budget` command group lacks a `create` subcommand in this version, the SOP leverages `az rest` to invoke the Microsoft.Consumption/budgets PUT API directly (api-version 2021-10-01). This creates a Monthly budget of $5 USD with two notification triggers: 'Actual_GreaterThan_5_USD' (triggers when actual spend > $5) and 'Forecasted_GreaterThan_5_USD' (triggers when forecasted spend > $5). Notifications are sent to Owner/Contributor roles and a placeholder email (admin@example.com) which must be updated to the actual recipient. Device code login is used for headless server authentication.", "safetyChecks": [{"check": "az account show --query \\"{Name:name, ID:id, State:state}\\" -o table", "passed": true}, {"check": "az consumption b