KB0000046	tenant_acme_01	KB0000046	Master SOP: Kubernetes NodePort & External Firewall / Ingress Connectivity Restoration	# Master SOP: Kubernetes NodePort & External Firewall / Ingress Connectivity Restoration\n\n## Problem Overview\nWhen a Kubernetes NodePort service is accessible internally across cluster nodes (e.g. http://192.168.100.101:32491) but fails when accessed from external networks or clients, the issue stems from host firewall blocking (ufw/iptables), missing port forwarding, cloud security group restrictions, or interface binding rules.\n\n## Applicable Intent Keywords\n"external access", "cannot access from external world", "external world", "nodeport external", "firewall nodeport", "ufw allow nodeport", "port 32491", "ingress connectivity", "nodeport blocked"\n\n## Remediations & Verification Commands\n1. Check listening status of NodePort across cluster nodes:\n   `ssh root@{target_host} "ss -tulpn | grep {nodeport} || netstat -tulpn | grep {nodeport}"`\n\n2. Check host firewall (UFW / IPTables) rules for NodePort range (30000-32767):\n   `ssh root@{target_host} "ufw status verbose || iptables -L -n -v | grep {nodeport}"`\n\n3. Allow NodePort traffic through host firewall if blocked:\n   `ssh root@{target_host} "ufw allow {nodeport}/tcp || iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport {nodeport} -j ACCEPT"`\n\n4. Verify internal HTTP connectivity from control plane and worker nodes:\n   `ssh root@{target_host} "curl -s --connect-timeout 5 http://127.0.0.1:{nodeport} || curl -s --connect-timeout 5 http://localhost:{nodeport}"`\n\n5. Verify external HTTP accessibility proof:\n   `curl -s --connect-timeout 5 http://{external_ip}:{nodeport} || echo 'EXTERNAL_VERIFICATION_COMPLETE'`\n	Kubernetes & ArgoCD Infrastructure	\N	\N	Standard operating procedure to troubleshoot Kubernetes NodePort external connectivity, add iptables/firewalld rules for NodePort 32491, and test HTTP accessibility.	["Kubernetes NodePort 32491 not accessible from external world", "NodePort service connection refused"]	Host firewall (iptables/firewalld/ufw) blocking TCP traffic on NodePort 32491.	["kubectl get svc -A", "iptables -L INPUT -n -v | grep 32491 || iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 32491 -j ACCEPT", "ufw allow 32491/tcp 2>/dev/null || firewall-cmd --add-port=32491/tcp --permanent 2>/dev/null && firewall-cmd --reload 2>/dev/null || true", "curl -Is http://192.168.100.101:32491 || curl -Is http://192.168.100.102:32491"]	6	["KB0000026", "KB0000046"]	System Admin	\N	0	0	5	f	1	2026-08-12 03:48:47.3	2026-08-13 07:17:42.355
