ostgres-prod-01 has presented an expired X.509 certificate during IKE_AUTH negotiation, causing remote peer authentication failures and tunnel teardown. The certificate file in /etc/ipsec.d/certs/ has a notAfter date prior to the current system time, requiring immediate replacement with a newly issued certificate and private key pair, followed by a daemon reload to flush the cached credential.", "category": "Server - Kernel & OS Patch", "symptoms": ["StrongSwan logs (/var/log/charon.log) show 'certificate validity check failed: certificate expired' and 'authentication of 'CN=vpn-gateway-prod' (myself) with RSA_EMSA_PKCS1_SHA2_256 failed' during IKE_SA_INIT.", "Remote peer logs indicate 'NO_PROPOSAL_CHOSEN' or 'AUTHENTICATION_FAILED' notify payloads received from postgres-prod-01 IP.", "Command 'ipsec listcerts' output displays the 'End Entity' certificate with a 'Not After' timestamp in the past (e.g., 'Aug 15 2024').", "Active IPsec SAs drop to zero for affected tunnels; 'ipsec statusall' shows no established CHILD_SAs for the gateway connection profile."], "createdAt": "2026-08-01T09:42:31.848Z", "modelUsed": "NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B / Meta Llama 3.3 70B (NIM)", "rootCause": "The X.509 end-entity certificate used by the StrongSwan IKE daemon (charon) for gateway authentication expired at 00:00 UTC today. The certificate lifecycle management process failed to trigger renewal via the internal PKI (Vault/ADCS) 30 days prior, leaving the gateway presenting an invalid credential during IKEv2 authentication.", "viewCount": 1, "helpfulCount": 0, "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@postgres-prod-01", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"cd /etc/ipsec.d && openssl x509 -in certs/vpn-gateway-prod.pem -text -noout | grep -A2 'Validity'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"curl -k -H \\\\\\"X-Vault-Token: $(cat /root/.vault-token)\\\\\\" -X POST -d '{\\\\\\"common_name\\\\\\": \\\\\\"vpn-gateway-prod\\\\\\", \\\\\\"ttl\\\\\\": \\\\\\"8760h\\\\\\"}' https://vault.internal:8200/v1/pki/issue/vpn-gateway | jq -r '.data.certificate' > certs/vpn-gateway-prod.pem.new && curl -k -H \\\\\\"X-Vault-Token: $(cat /root/.vault-token)\\\\\\" -X POST -d '{\\\\\\"common_name\\\\\\": \\\\\\"vpn-gateway-prod\\\\\\"}' https://vault.internal:8200/v1/pki/issue/vpn-gateway | jq -r '.data.private_key' > private/vpn-gateway-prod.key.new\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"chmod 640 certs/vpn-gateway-prod.pem.new private/vpn-gateway-prod.key.new && chown root:ipsec certs/vpn-gateway-prod.pem.new private/vpn-gateway-prod.key.new && mv certs/vpn-gateway-prod.pem.new certs/vpn-gateway-prod.pem && mv private/vpn-gateway-prod.key.new private/vpn-gateway-prod.key\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ipsec rereadcerts && ipsec reload && ipsec statusall | grep -A5 'vpn-gateway-prod'\\""], "configurationItem": "postgres-prod-01", "sourceIncidentIds": ["INC0000081", "INC0000082", "INC0000083", "INC0000084", "INC0000085", "INC0000086", "INC0000087", "INC0000088", "INC0000089", "INC0000090"], "workNotesAnalyzedCount": 10}, {"id": "KB0000009", "title": "Kubernetes Node & Kubelet Recovery SOP", "author": "🤖 NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B Knowledge Agent", "number": "KB0000009", "summary": "Guidance for resolving Kubelet daemon failures, node NotReady states, and container runtime communication issues.", "category": "User Error - Training Provided", "symptoms": ["Kubernetes worker node status transitions to 'NotReady'.", "Kubelet service fails to start or reports connection refused to API server.", "Container runtime endpoints timed out in logs."], "createdAt": "2026-08-01T09:41:59.592Z", "modelUsed": "NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B / Meta Llama 3.3 70B (NIM)", "rootCause": "Kubelet certificate expiration, swap space enabled blocking kubelet startup, or containerd service crash.", "viewCount": 1, "helpfulCount": 0, "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Inspect kubelet status: 'systemctl status kubelet'\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Check containerd state and restart if dead: 'systemctl restart conta